<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>🏛️ Kypria-LLC Canon Audit Tool</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e, #16213e);
            color: #e94560;
            min-height: 100vh;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
            border-radius: 15px;
            padding: 30px;
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            border: 1px solid rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.2);
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        .header h1 {
            color: #f39c12;
            font-size: 2.5em;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(243, 156, 18, 0.5);
        }

        .header p {
            color: #bdc3c7;
            font-size: 1.1em;
        }

        .auth-section {
            background: rgba(52, 73, 94, 0.3);
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            border-left: 4px solid #e94560;
        }

        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
            color: #ecf0f1;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        input, select {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 12px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.3);
            border-radius: 5px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
            color: #ecf0f1;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        input:focus, select:focus {
            outline: none;
            border-color: #f39c12;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(243, 156, 18, 0.3);
        }

        .btn {
            background: linear-gradient(45deg, #e94560, #f39c12);
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 12px 25px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
            font-weight: 600;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
        }

        .btn:hover {
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.4);
        }

        .btn:disabled {
            opacity: 0.6;
            cursor: not-allowed;
            transform: none;
        }

        .results {
            margin-top: 30px;
        }

        .repo-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
            gap: 20px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .repo-card {
            background: rgba(52, 73, 94, 0.4);
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 20px;
            border-left: 4px solid #3498db;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .repo-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }

        .repo-card.compliant {
            border-left-color: #27ae60;
        }

        .repo-card.non-compliant {
            border-left-color: #e74c3c;
        }

        .repo-card.partial {
            border-left-color: #f39c12;
        }

        .repo-name {
            font-size: 1.2em;
            font-weight: 600;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            color: #ecf0f1;
        }

        .repo-status {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .status-badge {
            padding: 4px 12px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            font-size: 12px;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .status-badge.compliant {
            background: rgba(39, 174, 96, 0.2);
            color: #27ae60;
            border: 1px solid #27ae60;
        }

        .status-badge.non-compliant {
            background: rgba(231, 76, 60, 0.2);
            color: #e74c3c;
            border: 1px solid #e74c3c;
        }

        .status-badge.partial {
            background: rgba(243, 156, 18, 0.2);
            color: #f39c12;
            border: 1px solid #f39c12;
        }

        .workflow-list {
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #bdc3c7;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }

        .summary {
            background: rgba(52, 73, 94, 0.3);
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .summary-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr));
            gap: 20px;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }

        .summary-item {
            background: rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.1);
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }

        .summary-number {
            font-size: 2em;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #f39c12;
        }

        .summary-label {
            font-size: 0.9em;
            color: #bdc3c7;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
        }

        .loading {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 40px;
        }

        .spinner {
            border: 4px solid rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.3);
            border-top: 4px solid #e94560;
            border-radius: 50%;
            width: 40px;
            height: 40px;
            animation: spin 1s linear infinite;
            margin: 0 auto 20px;
        }

        @keyframes spin {
            0% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
            100% { transform: rotate(360deg); }
        }

        .error {
            background: rgba(231, 76, 60, 0.2);
            color: #e74c3c;
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border-left: 4px solid #e74c3c;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }

        .report-section {
            margin-top: 30px;
            background: rgba(52, 73, 94, 0.2);
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        .report-content {
            background: #2c3e50;
            padding: 15px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
            font-size: 12px;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            max-height: 400px;
            overflow-y: auto;
            border: 1px solid rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.3);
        }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .repo-grid {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            }
            
            .summary-grid {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>🏛️ Kypria-LLC Canon Audit Tool</h1>
            <p>Legendary automation reconnaissance across your GitHub organization</p>
        </div>

        <div class="auth-section">
            <h3 style="color: #f39c12; margin-bottom: 15px;">🔑 Authentication & Configuration</h3>
            
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="pat">GitHub Personal Access Token:</label>
                <input type="password" id="pat" placeholder="ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx">
                <small style="color: #bdc3c7; font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px; display: block;">
                    Requires: repo, read:org permissions. <a href="https://github.com/settings/tokens/new" target="_blank" style="color: #f39c12;">Create token</a>
                </small>
            </div>

            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="organization">Organization:</label>
                <input type="text" id="organization" value="Kypria-LLC" placeholder="Organization name">
            </div>

            <button class="btn" onclick="startAudit()">⚡ Begin Reconnaissance</button>
        </div>

        <div id="results" class="results" style="display: none;">
            <div id="summary" class="summary"></div>
            <div id="repositories" class="repo-grid"></div>
            <div id="report" class="report-section" style="display: none;">
                <h3 style="color: #f39c12; margin-bottom: 15px;">📋 Generated Report</h3>
                <button class="btn" onclick="downloadReport()" style="margin-bottom: 15px;">⬇️ Download Report</button>
                <div id="reportContent" class="report-content"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="loading" class="loading" style="display: none;">
            <div class="spinner"></div>
            <p>🔍 Scanning repositories...</p>
        </div>

        <div id="error" class="error" style="display: none;"></div>
    </div>

    <script>
        let auditData = {};
        let reportContent = '';

        async function startAudit() {
            const pat = document.getElementById('pat').value.trim();
            const org = document.getElementById('organization').value.trim();

            if (!pat || !org) {
                showError('Please provide both GitHub PAT and organization name');
                return;
            }

            document.getElementById('loading').style.display = 'block';
            document.getElementById('results').style.display = 'none';
            document.getElementById('error').style.display = 'none';

            try {
                const repos = await fetchRepositories(pat, org);
                const auditResults = await auditRepositories(pat, org, repos);
                
                auditData = {
                    organization: org,
                    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
                    repositories: auditResults,
                    summary: calculateSummary(auditResults)
                };

                displayResults(auditData);
                generateReport(auditData);
                
            } catch (error) {
                showError(`Audit failed: ${error.message}`);
            } finally {
                document.getElementById('loading').style.display = 'none';
            }
        }

        async function fetchRepositories(pat, org) {
            const response = await fetch(`https://api.github.com/orgs/${org}/repos?per_page=100`, {
                headers: {
                    'Authorization': `token ${pat}`,
                    'Accept': 'application/vnd.github.v3+json'
                }
            });

            if (!response.ok) {
                throw new Error(`Failed to fetch repositories: ${response.status} ${response.statusText}`);
            }

            return await response.json();
        }

        async function auditRepositories(pat, org, repos) {
            const results = [];

            for (const repo of repos) {
                try {
                    const workflows = await fetchWorkflows(pat, org, repo.name);
                    const branches = await fetchBranches(pat, org, repo.name);
                    
                    const hasCanonCI = workflows.some(w => 
                        w.name.toLowerCase().includes('canon') || 
                        w.name.toLowerCase().includes('kypria')
                    );

                    const status = hasCanonCI ? 'compliant' : 
                                workflows.length > 0 ? 'partial' : 'non-compliant';

                    results.push({
                        name: repo.name,
                        url: repo.html_url,
                        private: repo.private,
                        defaultBranch: repo.default_branch,
                        workflows: workflows,
                        workflowCount: workflows.length,
                        hasCanonCI: hasCanonCI,
                        status: status,
                        branches: branches
                    });

                } catch (error) {
                    results.push({
                        name: repo.name,
                        url: repo.html_url,
                        private: repo.private,
                        status: 'error',
                        error: error.message
                    });
                }

                // Add delay to avoid rate limiting
                await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));
            }

            return results;
        }

        async function fetchWorkflows(pat, org, repo) {
            try {
                const response = await fetch(`https://api.github.com/repos/${org}/${repo}/actions/workflows`, {
                    headers: {
                        'Authorization': `token ${pat}`,
                        'Accept': 'application/vnd.github.v3+json'
                    }
                });

                if (!response.ok) return [];
                
                const data = await response.json();
                return data.workflows || [];
            } catch (error) {
                return [];
            }
        }

        async function fetchBranches(pat, org, repo) {
            try {
                const response = await fetch(`https://api.github.com/repos/${org}/${repo}/branches`, {
                    headers: {
                        'Authorization': `token ${pat}`,
                        'Accept': 'application/vnd.github.v3+json'
                    }
                });

                if (!response.ok) return [];
                
                return await response.json();
            } catch (error) {
                return [];
            }
        }

        function calculateSummary(repositories) {
            const total = repositories.length;
            const compliant = repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'compliant').length;
            const partial = repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'partial').length;
            const nonCompliant = repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'non-compliant').length;
            const errors = repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'error').length;

            return {
                total,
                compliant,
                partial,
                nonCompliant,
                errors,
                complianceRate: total > 0 ? Math.round((compliant / total) * 100) : 0
            };
        }

        function displayResults(data) {
            const { repositories, summary } = data;

            // Display summary
            const summaryEl = document.getElementById('summary');
            summaryEl.innerHTML = `
                <h3 style="color: #f39c12; margin-bottom: 20px;">📊 Canon Compliance Summary</h3>
                <div class="summary-grid">
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div class="summary-number">${summary.total}</div>
                        <div class="summary-label">Total Repos</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div class="summary-number">${summary.compliant}</div>
                        <div class="summary-label">✅ Compliant</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div class="summary-number">${summary.partial}</div>
                        <div class="summary-label">🔄 Partial</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div class="summary-number">${summary.nonCompliant}</div>
                        <div class="summary-label">❌ Missing</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="summary-item">
                        <div class="summary-number">${summary.complianceRate}%</div>
                        <div class="summary-label">Compliance Rate</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            `;

            // Display repositories
            const reposEl = document.getElementById('repositories');
            reposEl.innerHTML = repositories.map(repo => `
                <div class="repo-card ${repo.status}">
                    <div class="repo-name">
                        <a href="${repo.url}" target="_blank" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">
                            ${repo.name} ${repo.private ? '🔒' : '🌐'}
                        </a>
                    </div>
                    <div class="repo-status">
                        <span class="status-badge ${repo.status}">
                            ${repo.status === 'compliant' ? '✅ Canon Ready' : 
                              repo.status === 'partial' ? '🔄 Needs Canon' : 
                              repo.status === 'non-compliant' ? '❌ No Workflows' : 
                              '⚠️ Error'}
                        </span>
                        <span style="font-size: 12px; color: #bdc3c7;">
                            ${repo.workflowCount || 0} workflows
                        </span>
                    </div>
                    ${repo.workflows ? `
                        <div class="workflow-list">
                            <strong>Workflows:</strong><br>
                            ${repo.workflows.slice(0, 3).map(w => `• ${w.name}`).join('<br>')}
                            ${repo.workflows.length > 3 ? `<br>• +${repo.workflows.length - 3} more` : ''}
                        </div>
                    ` : ''}
                    ${repo.error ? `<div style="color: #e74c3c; font-size: 12px; margin-top: 10px;">Error: ${repo.error}</div>` : ''}
                </div>
            `).join('');

            document.getElementById('results').style.display = 'block';
            document.getElementById('report').style.display = 'block';
        }

        function generateReport(data) {
            const timestamp = new Date().toLocaleString();
            const { repositories, summary, organization } = data;

            reportContent = `# 🏛️ ${organization} Canon Compliance Report

**Generated:** ${timestamp}
**Tool:** Kypria-LLC Canon Audit Tool
**Organization:** ${organization}

## 📊 Executive Summary

| Metric | Count | Percentage |
|--------|-------|------------|
| Total Repositories | ${summary.total} | 100% |
| ✅ Canon Compliant | ${summary.compliant} | ${Math.round((summary.compliant/summary.total)*100)}% |
| 🔄 Partial Compliance | ${summary.partial} | ${Math.round((summary.partial/summary.total)*100)}% |
| ❌ Non-Compliant | ${summary.nonCompliant} | ${Math.round((summary.nonCompliant/summary.total)*100)}% |
| ⚠️ Audit Errors | ${summary.errors} | ${Math.round((summary.errors/summary.total)*100)}% |

**Overall Compliance Rate: ${summary.complianceRate}%**

## 📋 Repository Details

| Repository | Status | Workflows | Canon CI | Notes |
|------------|--------|-----------|----------|-------|
${repositories.map(repo => 
`| [${repo.name}](${repo.url}) | ${getStatusEmoji(repo.status)} ${repo.status} | ${repo.workflowCount || 0} | ${repo.hasCanonCI ? '✅' : '❌'} | ${repo.private ? '🔒 Private' : '🌐 Public'} |`
).join('\n')}

## 🎯 Deployment Targets

### 🔴 High Priority (No Workflows)
${repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'non-compliant').map(r => `- **${r.name}**: No CI/CD automation present`).join('\n') || 'None'}

### 🟡 Medium Priority (Missing Canon)
${repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'partial').map(r => `- **${r.name}**: Has ${r.workflowCount} workflows but missing Canon CI`).join('\n') || 'None'}

### 🟢 Canon Compliant
${repositories.filter(r => r.status === 'compliant').map(r => `- **${r.name}**: Canon CI deployed and active`).join('\n') || 'None'}

## 🚀 Recommended Actions

${summary.complianceRate < 50 ? 
`### 🔴 Critical Actions Required
- Deploy Canon CI workflow to ${summary.nonCompliant + summary.partial} repositories
- Establish organization-wide workflow templates
- Implement branch protection policies` :
summary.complianceRate < 90 ?
`### 🟡 Enhancement Phase
- Complete Canon CI deployment to remaining ${summary.nonCompliant + summary.partial} repositories  
- Standardize existing workflows with Canon templates
- Review and update security policies` :
`### 🟢 Maintenance Phase
- Monitor compliance with automated reporting
- Evolve Canon templates based on organizational needs
- Consider advanced automation features`}

## 📚 Next Steps

1. **Deploy Canon CI** to repositories marked as non-compliant or partial
2. **Configure branch protection** rules across all repositories
3. **Establish reusable workflows** in a central canon repository
4. **Schedule regular audits** to maintain compliance

---
*Report generated by Kypria-LLC Canon Audit Tool — Legendary automation reconnaissance* 🏛️`;

            document.getElementById('reportContent').textContent = reportContent;
        }

        function getStatusEmoji(status) {
            switch(status) {
                case 'compliant': return '✅';
                case 'partial': return '🔄';
                case 'non-compliant': return '❌';
                case 'error': return '⚠️';
                default: return '❓';
            }
        }

        function downloadReport() {
            const blob = new Blob([reportContent], { type: 'text/markdown' });
            const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
            const a = document.createElement('a');
            a.href = url;
            a.download = `kypria_canon_audit_${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,19).replace(/:/g,'-')}.md`;
            document.body.appendChild(a);
            a.click();
            document.body.removeChild(a);
            URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
        }

        function showError(message) {
            const errorEl = document.getElementById('error');
            errorEl.textContent = message;
            errorEl.style.display = 'block';
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
